From 972312a4cae60c31cb7977d80657e3f71cdad95f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:47:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: the drop control compares only pictures whose
 times are known

CDVDVideoCodecFFmpeg::CDropControl learns the time between two pictures from
the first ones it sees, and once it knows it (VALID) checks every picture
against it. That check computed std::abs(pts - m_lastPTS - m_diffPTS) without
looking at whether either time was known. After a seek, Reset(false) keeps the
estimate but forgets the last time (AV_NOPTS_VALUE, INT64_MIN), so the first
picture after every seek computed pts - INT64_MIN: a signed overflow, undefined
behaviour. In practice it wraps, the result is taken for a jump, and the
picture counts as one of the six deviations in a row after which the estimate
is thrown away. A picture without a time (AV_NOPTS_VALUE) does the same.

Compare only when both times are known, as the learning step before it
already does: a picture with nothing to be compared with neither counts as a
deviation nor clears the deviations counted. Every picture with two known
times is checked as before.

Found by the host test of the cadence of H.264 MVC (a seek through Reset() as
the player does it, under the undefined-behaviour sanitizer); it concerns every
stream, not only MVC. Kodi master has the same code.
---
 .../cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp
index 233601e..1a48abe 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp
@@ -280,7 +280,9 @@ void CDVDVideoCodecFFmpeg::CDropControl::Process(int64_t pts, bool drop)
       }
     }
   }
-  else if (m_state == VALID && !drop)
+  // Hades: only a picture whose time and the time of the picture before it are known is compared
+  // (after Reset(false), a seek, the last time is not: pts - AV_NOPTS_VALUE overflowed)
+  else if (m_state == VALID && !drop && pts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE && m_lastPTS != AV_NOPTS_VALUE)
   {
     if (std::abs(pts - m_lastPTS - m_diffPTS) > m_diffPTS * 0.2)
     {
